          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em partial function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: A \to B
            is like a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            except that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x)
            may not be defined for every element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multi-valued+function"} multi-valued function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x)
            may have several possible values.)
          %p
            In some fields (including secondary-school mathematics even today), functions are often considered to be partial by default, requiring one to specify a
            %em total
            function otherwise. As category-theoretic and type-theoretic formalisation spreads, this is difficult to treat as the basic concept, and the most modern idea is that a function must be total. If you want partial functions, then you can get them in terms of total functions as below.
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %h3#in_type_theory In type theory
          %h4#as_functions As functions
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-sets"} h-sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %strong partial function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is an
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-proposition"} h-proposition
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_f
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            which states whether
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is defined for element
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:A
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mi f
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A, p:P_f \vdash f:B
          %p
            If the dependent type theory has
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+types"} function types
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum+types"} dependent sum types
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo )
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:\left(\sum_{a:A} P_f(a)\right) \to B
          %h4#as_partial_anafunctions As partial anafunctions
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %strong partial anafunction
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+family"} type family
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi B
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\colon A, y \colon B \vdash R(x, y) \; \mathrm{type}
            which comes with a family of witnesses
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isProp
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo :
                        %mi B
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \colon A \vdash p(x) \colon \mathrm{isProp}\left(\sum_{y:B} R(x, y) \right)
          %p
            that for each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/term"} element
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\colon A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum+type"} dependent sum type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi B
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{y \colon B} R(x, y)
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mere+proposition"} mere proposition
          %p
            Historically, partial anafunctions are called
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functional+relations"} functional relations
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation"} relation
            only for those
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+families"} type families
            which are valued in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mere+propositions"} mere propositions
          %p For any partial anafunction, there is a partial function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isContr
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo :
                        %mi B
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo )
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A, p:\mathrm{isContr}\left(\sum_{y:B} R(x, y) \right) \vdash f(x, p):B
          %p which could be written as the function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isContr
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo :
                        %mi B
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo )
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:\sum_{x:A} \mathrm{isContr}\left(\sum_{y:B} R(x, y) \right) \to B
          %p
            since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mi B
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{y:B} R(x, y)
            is already a proposition, one could simply use
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mi B
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A, p:\sum_{y:B} R(x, y) \vdash f(x, p):B
          %p instead, and by the rules of dependent sum types, it becomes
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A, y:B, p:R(x, y) \vdash f(x, y, p):B
          %p on the other side, the function can be written as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo :
                        %mi B
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo )
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:\left(\sum_{x:A} \sum_{y:B} R(x, y) \right) \to B
          %h4#examples  Examples
          %p There are multiple examples of partial functions in mathematics.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reciprocal+function"} reciprocal function
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            is only defined on the real numbers apart from zero, and so is given by the following rules:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msup
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash \mathbb{R} \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma, x:\mathbb{R}, p:\vert x \vert \gt 0 \vdash {(-)}^{-1}:\mathbb{R}}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} recipax
                      %mo :
                      %mi x
                      %mo ⋅
                      %msup
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mi ℝ
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash \mathbb{R} \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma, x:\mathbb{R}, p:\vert x \vert \gt 0 \vdash \mathrm{recipax}:x \cdot {(x, p)}^{-1} =_\mathbb{R} 1}
          %p
            The reciprocal function is given by the partial anafunction
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi y
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mi ℝ
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \cdot y =_\mathbb{R} 1
          %p
            Another example is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+square+root"} metric square root
            on the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mi x
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msqrt
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash \mathbb{R} \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma, x:\mathbb{R}, p:x \geq 0 \vdash \sqrt{-}:\mathbb{R}}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mi x
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} sqrtax
                      %mo :
                      %msup
                        %msqrt
                          %mrow
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi p
                        %mn 2
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mi ℝ
                      %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash \mathbb{R} \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma, x:\mathbb{R}, p:x \geq 0 \vdash \mathrm{sqrtax}:\sqrt{x, p}^2 =_\mathbb{R} x}
          %p
            In both cases, the witness
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            is usually left implicit in informal notation, and the partial function is written as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {x}^{-1}
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msqrt
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sqrt{x}
          %h3#in_category_theory In category theory
          %h4#DefinitionInSets In the category of sets
          %p
            Given
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %strong partial function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            consists a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and a (total) function from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} span
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi D
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ↙
                            %mi ι
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo ↘
                            %mi f
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array {
                  \&amp;                &amp; D \\
                  \&amp; \swarrow_\iota &amp;   &amp; \searrow^f \\
                  A &amp;                &amp;   &amp;            &amp; B \\
                  }
          %p
            of total functions, where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ι
                  %mo :
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota: D \to A
            is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injection"} injection
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multi-valued+function"} multi-valued function
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            are called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/source"} source
            and
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target"} target
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            as usual; then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            is the
            %strong domain
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ι
                  %mo :
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota: D \to A
            is the
            %strong inclusion
            of the domain into the source. By abuse of notation, the partial function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is conflated with the (total) function
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: D \to B
          %p
            Notice that the induced function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mo ×
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \to A \times B
            is an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injection"} injection
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functional+relation"} functional relation
            seen from a different point of view.
          %p
            We consider two partial functions (with the same given source and target) to be
            %strong equal
            if there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
            between their domains that makes the obvious diagrams commute. You can get this automatically in a traditional set theory by requiring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            to be literally a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            (with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ι
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota
            the inclusion map).
          %h4#DefinitionGeneralAbstract General abstract
          %h5#in_terms_of_spans In terms of spans
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
            %strong partial map
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            may be defined to be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} span
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi D
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mi i
                          %mo ↙
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo ↘
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi f
                        %mtd
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
